-- title:
--   Stalks over the vertex of uv=wvarpi^E have dimension ≥ 2
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, and let $\varpi \in O$ be such that the maximal ideal of $O$ equals the principal ideal $(\varpi)$. Let $E$ be a natural number with $E \ge 1$, let $w$ be a unit of $O$, and let $a \in O$ be the element $a = w\varpi^{E}$. Consider the quotient ring $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,O\,a = O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - a)$, written as a quotient of the polynomial ring in the variable set $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - a$, and the affine scheme $\operatorname{Spec}$ of this ring, denoted `CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme a`. Let $m$ be a point of this scheme, i.e. a prime ideal $\mathfrak p_m$ of the quotient ring, and assume that both distinguished elements `CrossingQuotient.U a` and `CrossingQuotient.V a` of the quotient ring — the two coordinate classes, characterised by the universal property of the crossing quotient and satisfying $UV = a$ — lie in $\mathfrak p_m$. The conclusion is that the Krull dimension of the stalk of the structure presheaf of `CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme a` at $m$ is at least $2$, as an inequality in $\mathbb{N}_\infty$ extended by $\bot$.
--
--   This is the local dimension estimate at a point of the plane crossing $uv = w\varpi^{E}$ lying over the vertex, where both coordinate functions vanish: the local ring there has a chain of primes of length at least two. It supplies the dimension input for the identification of the adic completion of such a stalk with the standard $uv$-crossing model, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_crossingScheme_uvCrossingModel_of_mem_asIdeal`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_crossingScheme_uvCrossingModel_of_mem_asIdeal).
